  "slug": "pharmacology-validation-6359",
  "summary": "scSpatial curates over 1800 tissue sections from 630 projects, and 4D-atlas standardizes 1629 slices, so cell-level reuse depends on searchable frameworks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the packaging of single-cell and spatial transcriptomic data into queryable resources that attach external evidence to cell-level observations. Scale is central: scSpatial curates over 1800 tissue sections from 630 projects, and 4D-atlas standardizes 1629 slices across 88 time points and six species. Layered evidence includes protein interaction and cell-cell communication networks in LiverHomo and CCCView, TF regulon activity across 1322 slices in SpatialRegNet, and isoform, poly(A) and allelic evidence in scTHREAD. RFind-sc projects cells onto axes defined by external gene signatures and Perturb-seq knockouts, while an 11-method segmentation benchmark across 15 spatial datasets addresses the upstream cell-definition step. Some entries, such as TAPESTRY, rpMeta and ConcuRx, fall outside single-cell scope. What is new is the integration of cell-resolved and spatial layers within searchable frameworks.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-27"
}
